Description: Open a URL from the command line in a window of its own when external links open in new windows.
 When Firefox starts with a URL, as when a link is opened from another application while Firefox is not running,
 and restores the previous session at startup, the session store restores the first window of the saved session
 into the window opened for the URL, so the URL becomes a tab of that window, on whichever workspace it returns to.
 This happens also when browser.link.open_newwindow.override.external (or browser.link.open_newwindow, which it
 falls back to) opens external links in a new window, as they do while Firefox runs. When the preference opens
 them in a new window, the window opened for the URL now keeps only it, every saved window is restored into a new
 window, and the window with the URL is the one focused afterwards.
 .
 On Wayland every window opened during startup session restore waits hidden until it is restored, and a window
 which is not restored is shown when session restore finishes (wayland-session-restore-show-waiting-windows.patch).
 The window with the URL is thus shown after the restored ones, so the compositor places it on the current
 workspace and focuses it after any restored window there.
 .
 Related to Mozilla bug 1565050: with external links opening in a tab, the URL opens in the first window of the
 saved session rather than in the last used one.
